# Title VI — Committee on Environment and Public Works

**Sec. 60001. Rescission of funding for clean heavy-duty vehicles.**
This section rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out section 132 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7432), which relates to clean heavy-duty vehicles. Any money appropriated for this program that has not yet been committed is permanently withdrawn.

**Sec. 60002. Repeal of Greenhouse Gas Reduction Fund.**
Section 134 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7434), which established the Greenhouse Gas Reduction Fund, is repealed in its entirety. Additionally, all unobligated balances of funds made available for that program (as of the day before enactment) are rescinded.

**Sec. 60003. Rescission of funding for diesel emissions reductions.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60104 of Public Law 117-169 (the Inflation Reduction Act, 136 Stat. 2067) for diesel emissions reductions are rescinded. Unspent appropriations for this program are eliminated.

**Sec. 60004. Rescission of funding to address air pollution.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60105 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2067) for addressing air pollution are rescinded. Unspent money for this air pollution program is withdrawn.

**Sec. 60005. Rescission of funding to address air pollution at schools.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60106 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2069) for addressing air pollution in schools are rescinded. Unspent school air quality monitoring/mitigation funds are eliminated.

**Sec. 60006. Rescission of funding for the low emissions electricity program.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out section 135 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7435), the low emissions electricity program, are rescinded. Unspent appropriations for this program are withdrawn.

**Sec. 60007. Rescission of funding for section 211(o) of the Clean Air Act.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60108 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2070), which funded activities under Clean Air Act section 211(o) (relating to fuels and fuel additives), are rescinded.

**Sec. 60008. Rescission of funding for implementation of the American Innovation and Manufacturing Act.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60109 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2071) for implementing the American Innovation and Manufacturing Act (which phases down hydrofluorocarbons) are rescinded.

**Sec. 60009. Rescission of funding for enforcement technology and public information.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60110 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2071) for enforcement technology and public information are rescinded. Unspent appropriations for these EPA activities are eliminated.

**Sec. 60010. Rescission of funding for greenhouse gas corporate reporting.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60111 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2072) for greenhouse gas corporate reporting are rescinded. Unspent funds for this reporting program are withdrawn.

**Sec. 60011. Rescission of funding for environmental product declaration assistance.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60112 of Public Law 117-169 (42 U.S.C. 4321 note; 136 Stat. 2072) for environmental product declaration assistance are rescinded. This eliminates unspent funds that helped producers document the environmental footprint of their products.

**Sec. 60012. Rescission of funding for methane emissions and waste reduction incentive program for petroleum and natural gas systems.**
Subsection (a) rescinds all unobligated balances of funds made available under subsections (a) and (b) of Clean Air Act section 136 (42 U.S.C. 7436), the methane emissions reduction incentive program for petroleum and natural gas systems. Subsection (b) amends Clean Air Act section 136(g) to extend the waste emissions charge period from calendar year 2024 to calendar year 2034.

**Sec. 60013. Rescission of funding for greenhouse gas air pollution plans and implementation grants.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 137 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7437) for greenhouse gas air pollution plans and implementation grants are rescinded. Unspent appropriations for these state/tribal planning grants are eliminated.

**Sec. 60014. Rescission of funding for Environmental Protection Agency efficient, accurate, and timely reviews.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60115 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2077) for EPA's efficient, accurate, and timely reviews (permitting/NEPA-related review capacity) are rescinded.

**Sec. 60015. Rescission of funding for low-embodied carbon labeling for construction materials.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60116 of Public Law 117-169 (42 U.S.C. 4321 note; 136 Stat. 2077) for low-embodied carbon labeling of construction materials are rescinded. Unspent funds for this labeling program are withdrawn.

**Sec. 60016. Rescission of funding for environmental and climate justice block grants.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 138 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7438), which authorized environmental and climate justice block grants, are rescinded. Unspent grant funds for community-level environmental justice projects are eliminated.

**Sec. 60017. Rescission of funding for ESA recovery plans.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60301 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2079) for Endangered Species Act recovery plans are rescinded. Unspent appropriations for developing and implementing species recovery plans are withdrawn.

**Sec. 60018. Rescission of funding for environmental and climate data collection.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60401 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2079) for environmental and climate data collection are rescinded. Unspent funds for these data-gathering activities are eliminated.

**Sec. 60019. Rescission of neighborhood access and equity grant program.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 177 of title 23, United States Code, for the Neighborhood Access and Equity grant program are rescinded. This eliminates unspent highway-adjacent community improvement and equity grant funding.

**Sec. 60020. Rescission of funding for Federal building assistance.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60502 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083) for Federal building assistance (GSA transformation of federal buildings) are rescinded. Unspent appropriations for this program are withdrawn.

**Sec. 60021. Rescission of funding for low-carbon materials for Federal buildings.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60503 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083) for low-carbon materials in Federal buildings are rescinded. Unspent funds for procuring low-carbon construction materials for federal projects are eliminated.

**Sec. 60022. Rescission of funding for GSA emerging and sustainable technologies.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 60504 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083) for GSA's emerging and sustainable technologies program are rescinded. Unspent appropriations for this General Services Administration program are withdrawn.

**Sec. 60023. Rescission of environmental review implementation funds.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 178 of title 23, United States Code, for environmental review implementation are rescinded. This eliminates unspent Department of Transportation funding for implementing environmental reviews.

**Sec. 60024. Rescission of low-carbon transportation materials grants.**
All unobligated balances of funds made available under section 179 of title 23, United States Code, for low-carbon transportation materials grants are rescinded. Unspent grant funding for low-carbon materials in transportation projects is eliminated.

**Sec. 60025. John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts.**
This section appropriates $256,657,000 for fiscal year 2025, available until September 30, 2029, for capital repair, restoration, maintenance backlog, and security structures of the John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts building and site. Of this amount, not more than 3 percent may be used for administrative costs.

**Sec. 60026. Project sponsor opt-in fees for environmental reviews.**
This section adds new NEPA section 112, allowing a project sponsor to pay a fee to accelerate environmental assessments (EAs) or environmental impact statements (EISs). The sponsor submits a project description to the Council on Environmental Quality, which must notify the sponsor of the fee amount within 15 days; the fee is 125 percent of anticipated preparation costs (or supervision costs if the sponsor prepares the document itself under section 107(f)). Once the fee is paid, the EA must be completed within 180 days, and the EIS within 1 year of the notice of intent to prepare it. [end of text]


